	<translation id="5890206344045530832">Installer</translation>
	<translation id="2173278076276376488">This utility will help you install <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>JemaOS</ex></ph> onto the internal storage of this device.</translation>
	<translation id="5323182426977498659">Warning! This procedure is destructive and cannot be undone. Please note that we will not hold any responsibility for your potential data loss nor provide any urgent technical support, proceed at your own risk.</translation>
	<translation id="8517836015601969896">Full disk installation</translation>
	<translation id="7300045760790370189">Install <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>JemaOS</ex></ph> to occupy an entire hard disk, all data of the target hard disk will be wiped.</translation>
	<translation id="8762511733918256595">Multi-boot installation</translation>
	<translation id="248900698427753678">Install <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>JemaOS</ex></ph> to an existing partition of a hard disk, where <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>JemaOS</ex></ph> can exist in parallel with other OS. All data on the target partition will be wiped.</translation>
	<translation id="8445241586733258838"><ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>JemaOS</ex></ph> will be installed on your selected hard drive; all data on the target disk will be wiped.</translation>
	<translation id="4039091757234555415">Disk</translation>
	<translation id="7783580523889684697">No disk available</translation>
	<translation id="8217653566575018388">Installation completed</translation>
	<translation id="8846746259444262774">Installation failed</translation>
	<translation id="7263815009235541549">The installation has finished successfully. Please power off your device first, then remove any installation media, and power it on again to boot <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>JemaOS</ex></ph>.</translation>
	<translation id="3380151284134965398">Oops, something has gone wrong and the installation did not complete. Please retry the process. If the same error persists, please reach out for JemaOS Support with the above log.</translation>
	<translation id="4683944976188707627"><ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>JemaOS</ex></ph> will be installed on the selected partition of your hard drive. Under the current multi-boot scheme, this could only proceed if your device supports UEFI and your hard disks are formatted with GPT.</translation>
	<translation id="7831363758161884243">The target partition will be wiped; you also need to specify your active EFI partition (usually done automatically) as the Installer needs to modify system boot configurations.</translation>
	<translation id="5670799238446305550">Select <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>JemaOS</ex></ph> target partition</translation>
	<translation id="3695537760133394753">Partition</translation>
	<translation id="5610519566593708119">Select EFI partition</translation>
	<translation id="3367650349940010965">There are no partitions available for the selected disk</translation>
	<translation id="7453223384507098390">There are no EFI partitions available for the selected disk</translation>
	<translation id="1854532683465500847">The size of the selected partition is less than 20GB, installation may fail</translation>
	<translation id="4144613075340468247">The selected partition has been mounted to <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>JemaOS</ex></ph> multi-boot, install to it again may fail</translation>
	<translation id="5793361052649920836">After installation, how would you like to boot <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>JemaOS</ex></ph>?</translation>
	<translation id="4273235330352963866">Install and configure rEFInd for me (recommended)</translation>
	<translation id="1858708492548921044">rEFInd is a boot manager program that offers a nice graphical interface for OS boot options when your PC starts up, you will be able to choose your desired OS to boot with it. For more information regarding rEFInd, please refer to its homepage.</translation>
	<translation id="3861924051442564602">Add a UEFI boot menu option for me</translation>
	<translation id="8622370666798589804">When your PC starts up you may be able to enter the UEFI boot options menu (most likely by pressing a hotkey), this option adds <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>JemaOS</ex></ph> as an entry to that menu. (Only supports some models of BIOS and UEFI firmware).</translation>
	<translation id="1569398690544416170">Do nothing here, I will configure it myself</translation>
	<translation id="3554866444001249532">This installation script will only put necessary .efi files for booting <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>JemaOS</ex></ph> to your EFI partition, you will need to configure how to boot it by yourself.</translation>
	<translation id="7492832751164189534">Force quit</translation>
	<translation id="5159534860632584026">The installation process has been terminated</translation>
	<translation id="8686749782014838344">Failed to get disk information</translation>
	<translation id="5688543378771259173">The installation is being terminated...</translation>
	<translation id="5350452134936384991">Install in USB</translation>
	<translation id="8008470485414925603">Install <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>JemaOS</ex></ph> onto a USB disk; all data on the target USB disk will be wiped.</translation>
	<translation id="1270668145107456127"><ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>JemaOS</ex></ph> will be installed on your selected USB disk; all data on the target disk will be wiped.</translation>
	<translation id="5725593226060700263">No USB disk available</translation>
	<translation id="4357040841587078287">We have detected that you are running this copy of JemaOS from a downloaded image file. To utilise the most comprehensive support features (including Over-The-Air updates) that JemaOS can offer, we strongly recommend you launch the "Installer" function to perform a full-disk installation of JemaOS to a separate storage device.</translation>
	<translation id="1246398339704431302">You can <ph name="LINK_BEGIN">&amp;lt;span id="continue-anyway"&amp;gt;</ph>continue to use this copy of JemaOS anyway<ph name="LINK_END">&amp;lt;/span&amp;gt;</ph>, the installation process can be executed at a later stage in the system, however, all your data will be wiped after installation and you will begin again from this page.</translation>
	<translation id="3654532222088291133">Instead of entering your JemaOS account password to sign in, you can create a <ph name="DEVICE_TYPE">$1<ex>Chromebook</ex></ph> password for this device</translation>
	<translation id="8377684629839541977">Use JemaOS account password</translation>

